Concentrate. Concentrate. Concentrate.

1032
01:16:26,519 --> 01:16:29,408
Keep it in mind. Keep it in mind. Keep it in mind.

1033
01:16:32,800 --> 01:16:34,840
Come on. Find a pen. I have to find a pen.

1034
01:16:35,219 --> 01:16:36,239
Write this down.

1035
01:16:36,620 --> 01:16:38,680
Write this down, exactly what happened.

1036
01:16:38,750 --> 01:16:39,979
Gonna write down exactly what happened.

1037
01:16:40,149 --> 01:16:43,349
Come on. Come on. Come on. Find a pen. Jeez! Come on.

1038
01:16:43,959 --> 01:16:45,908
Okay, focus. Keep focused.

1039
01:16:46,890 --> 01:16:48,319
Keep... Keep it in mind.

1040
01:16:48,349 --> 01:16:50,389
Come on. Find a pen. Write this note.

1041
01:16:50,499 --> 01:16:52,859
Write down what happened. Write it down. Write it down. Come on.

1042
01:16:52,969 --> 01:16:55,129
Concentrate. Keep it in mind. Find a pen.

1043
01:17:03,379 --> 01:17:04,238
What happened?

1044
01:17:04,710 --> 01:17:06,369
What does it look like? He beat the shit out of me.

1045
01:17:06,710 --> 01:17:07,770
Who?

1046
01:17:08,209 --> 01:17:09,279
Who?

1047
01:17:09,899 --> 01:17:12,179
Fuck, Leonard. Dodd. Dodd beat the shit out of me.

1048
01:17:26,570 --> 01:17:28,399
It's Burt, from the front desk.

1049
01:17:31,740 --> 01:17:33,299
I know you said you didn't want any calls.

1050
01:17:33,509 --> 01:17:36,098
But this guy called. He's on the phone now. He says he's a cop.

1051
01:17:36,439 --> 01:17:37,208
-A cop? -Yeah.

1052
01:17:37,479 --> 01:17:41,338
And, uh, he says you're really gonna wanna know what he has to say, so...

1053
01:17:41,580 --> 01:17:42,979
I'm not too good on the phone.

1054
01:17:43,279 --> 01:17:44,609
I need to look people in the eye when I talk to them.

1055
01:17:44,750 --> 01:17:45,909
Well, what...

1056
01:17:50,489 --> 01:17:53,218
You can, um... You can crash on the couch.

1057
01:17:53,429 --> 01:17:54,258
It's comfortable.

1058
01:17:54,830 --> 01:17:55,779
Just have a seat.

1059
01:18:03,269 --> 01:18:04,998
So how long do you think it's gonna take you?

1060
01:18:07,009 --> 01:18:09,669
You told me you were looking for the guy who killed your wife?

1061
01:18:11,009 --> 01:18:14,938
Oh, well, that depends on if he's here in town or if he's moved on.

1062
01:18:15,079 --> 01:18:17,649
I have my file here.

1063
01:18:20,049 --> 01:18:21,349
Can I ask you something?

1064
01:18:21,660 --> 01:18:23,419
If you have all of that information,

1065
01:18:24,059 --> 01:18:26,179
then why haven't the police found him for you?

1066
01:18:27,489 --> 01:18:29,288
-Well, they're not looking for him. -Why not?

1067
01:18:30,399 --> 01:18:31,559
They don't think he exists.

1068
01:18:32,800 --> 01:18:34,929
You see, I told them what I remembered.

1069
01:18:35,539 --> 01:18:36,759
I was asleep.

1070
01:18:38,309 --> 01:18:39,329
Something woke me up.

1071
01:18:44,810 --> 01:18:47,909
Her side of the bed was cold. She'd obviously been out of bed for awhile.

1072
01:19:46,870 --> 01:19:48,569
There had to be a second man.

1073
01:19:49,579 --> 01:19:50,699
Somebody hit me from behind.

1074
01:19:50,979 --> 01:19:53,739
I remember. It's about the last thing that I do remember.

1075
01:19:54,049 --> 01:19:56,439
Look, the police did not believe me. If we check the police...

1076
01:19:56,620 --> 01:19:58,609
How do they explain what you do remember?

1077
01:19:58,989 --> 01:20:00,149
The gun and stuff.

1078
01:20:03,489 --> 01:20:04,549
John G. Was clever.

1079
01:20:05,660 --> 01:20:06,649
He was clever.

1080
01:20:07,059 --> 01:20:08,928
See, he took the dead man's gun

1081
01:20:09,399 --> 01:20:11,629
and replaced it with the sap that he hit me with.

1082
01:20:12,600 --> 01:20:14,730
He left my gun and he left the getaway car.

1083
01:20:14,999 --> 01:20:16,489
He gave the police a complete package.

1084
01:20:16,899 --> 01:20:20,239
The found the sap with my blood on it in the dead man's hand.

1085
01:20:21,479 --> 01:20:22,928
And they only found my gun.

1086
01:20:23,909 --> 01:20:25,569
They didn't need to look for anybody else.

1087
01:20:27,919 --> 01:20:31,109
I was the only guy who disagreed with the facts, and I had brain damage.

1088
01:20:31,620 --> 01:20:34,079
-See, the cops are not gonna believe someone in my condition. -Leonard,

1089
01:20:34,919 --> 01:20:37,519
You can stay here for a couple of days if it'll help you.

1090
01:20:41,730 --> 01:20:43,489
I have to go back to work.

1091
01:20:43,929 --> 01:20:47,419
So, um, just make yourself at home. You can watch TV, or...

1092
01:20:47,770 --> 01:20:50,159
you can have some food, whatever you want, okay?

1093
01:20:50,269 --> 01:20:51,268
Make yourself at home.

1094
01:20:52,209 --> 01:20:52,928
One thing.

1095
01:20:56,039 --> 01:20:57,499
Something to remember you by.

1096
01:20:57,949 --> 01:20:59,069
My name is Natalie.

1097
01:21:01,949 --> 01:21:03,379
"Natalie."

1098
01:21:20,169 --> 01:21:23,429
“记住杰克斯·萨米”

1099
01:21:36,579 --> 01:21:38,308
-What's wrong? -Somebody's come already.

1100
01:22:05,909 --> 01:22:07,439
“接我电话”

1101
01:22:27,569 --> 01:22:28,358
On the house.

1102
01:22:35,339 --> 01:22:36,799
My, you really do have a problem.

1103
01:22:37,880 --> 01:22:39,329
Just like that cop said.

1104
01:22:41,109 --> 01:22:42,269
Your condition.

1105
01:22:43,449 --> 01:22:44,819
Well, nobody's perfect.

1106
01:22:46,589 --> 01:22:49,508
What's the last thing that you do remember?

1107
01:22:53,089 --> 01:22:53,649
My wife.

1108
01:22:54,089 --> 01:22:54,859
That's sweet.

1109
01:22:55,359 --> 01:22:56,088
Dying.

1110
01:22:57,700 --> 01:22:59,219
I remember my wife dying.

1111
01:23:04,599 --> 01:23:06,528
Let me, um, get you another one.

1112
01:23:07,369 --> 01:23:08,829
I think this one's dusty.

1113
01:23:13,780 --> 01:23:15,539
-Why are you calling me? -What do you want?

1114
01:23:16,620 --> 01:23:17,670
I know you're a cop, but what do you want?

1115
01:23:17,750 --> 01:23:19,009
Have I done something wrong?

1116
01:23:20,389 --> 01:23:21,879
I don't know. Something bad, maybe.

1117
01:23:24,119 --> 01:23:26,489
Why are you asking me? I can't remember what I've done.

1118
01:23:26,660 --> 01:23:27,880
You wouldn't believe me anyway.

1119
01:23:28,660 --> 01:23:31,149
Because of my condition. You don't believe someone with this condition.

1120
01:23:31,730 --> 01:23:34,099
Nobody believed Sammy! I didn't even fucking believe Sammy!

1121
01:23:35,399 --> 01:23:36,729
"Ferdy's Bar."

1122
01:23:39,640 --> 01:23:41,629
"Come by after. Natalie."

1123
01:23:56,890 --> 01:23:57,949
I'll have a beer, please.

1124
01:23:58,329 --> 01:24:00,158
-What do you want? -A beer, please.

1125
01:24:00,259 --> 01:24:02,619
You can't just waltz in here dressed like that and ask for a beer.

1126
01:24:02,899 --> 01:24:04,919
-What, is there a dress code? -Why are you here?

1127
01:24:05,229 --> 01:24:06,359
I'm meeting someone called Natalie.

1128
01:24:06,800 --> 01:24:08,199
Well, that's me.

1129
01:24:08,539 --> 01:24:10,198
Yeah. We met before, right?

1130
01:24:11,840 --> 01:24:12,669
Then why am I here?

1131
01:24:12,939 --> 01:24:14,029
I don't know. Tell me.

1132
01:24:14,239 --> 01:24:16,799
I don't remember. I have no short-term memory. It's not amnesia.

1133
01:24:16,880 --> 01:24:18,239
Oh, you're the memory guy.

1134
01:24:18,479 --> 01:24:19,739
How do you know about me?

1135
01:24:20,249 --> 01:24:21,839
My boyfriend told me about you.

1136
01:24:22,179 --> 01:24:23,439
Yeah? Who's your boyfriend?

1137
01:24:24,179 --> 01:24:25,739
Jimmy Grants. Do you know him?

1138
01:24:27,189 --> 01:24:27,918
No.

1139
01:24:28,720 --> 01:24:29,919
Well, he knows you.

1140
01:24:30,690 --> 01:24:33,519
He told me about you. He said you were staying at the Discount.

1141
01:24:34,189 --> 01:24:36,749
In fact, a cop came by here earlier looking for you.

1142
01:24:37,499 --> 01:24:39,418
Said he was looking for a guy who can't remember anything,

1143
01:24:39,469 --> 01:24:41,559
wouldn't know how he got here or what he'd done.

1144
01:24:41,969 --> 01:24:43,769
Said I get a lot of guys around here like that.

1145
01:24:44,700 --> 01:24:47,800
Well, you know, chronic alcoholism is one cause of short-term memory loss.

1146
01:24:50,309 --> 01:24:51,268
Are you Teddy?

1147
01:24:51,549 --> 01:24:52,839
No. My name is Leonard.

1148
01:24:53,209 --> 01:24:55,409
-Did Teddy send you? -I don't know.

1149
01:24:56,549 --> 01:24:57,779
What's happened to Jimmy?

1150
01:24:58,319 --> 01:25:00,379
I don't know that either. Sorry.

1151
01:25:00,720 --> 01:25:01,679
You don't remember anything?

1152
01:25:01,989 --> 01:25:04,789
You don't remember where you've been or what you've just done.

1153
01:25:05,059 --> 01:25:07,119
No. I can't make new memories.

1154
01:25:07,489 --> 01:25:08,889
Everything just fades.

1155
01:25:09,229 --> 01:25:10,359
Then why did you come here?

1156
01:25:10,730 --> 01:25:11,820
I found this in my pocket.

1157
01:25:15,039 --> 01:25:16,399
Your pocket.

1158
01:25:41,599 --> 01:25:44,659
Bar bet. Care to contribute?

1159
01:25:44,999 --> 01:25:45,459
No, thanks.

1160
01:25:45,770 --> 01:25:46,559
It's for a lot of money.

1161
01:25:47,269 --> 01:25:49,789
Come on. Proceeds are going to charity. Help me out.

1162
01:26:21,199 --> 01:26:21,998
On the house.

1163
01:26:28,169 --> 01:26:30,559
It's completely fucked because nobody believes you.

1164
01:26:31,949 --> 01:26:34,569
It's amazing what a little brain damage will do for your credibility.

1165
01:26:35,149 --> 01:26:37,809
I guess it's some kind of poetic justice for not believing Sammy.

1166
01:26:38,179 --> 01:26:39,948
You know the truth about my condition, officer?

1167
01:26:40,989 --> 01:26:41,938
You don't know anything.

1168
01:26:42,919 --> 01:26:44,649
You feel angry, you don't know why.

1169
01:26:45,329 --> 01:26:47,889
You feel guilty, you have no idea why.

1170
01:26:49,059 --> 01:26:51,789
You could do anything and not have the faintest idea ten minutes later.

1171
01:26:52,099 --> 01:26:53,829
Like Sammy. I could have done something like Sammy.

1172
01:26:54,670 --> 01:26:55,459
I didn't tell you...

1173
01:26:56,369 --> 01:26:57,829
what happened to Sammy and his wife?

1174
01:26:59,670 --> 01:27:01,299
Well, she came to see me at my office.

1175
01:27:01,569 --> 01:27:02,968
I thought she was just trying to catch me off guard,

1176
01:27:03,009 --> 01:27:05,569
so I didn't tell her what I really thought, but I never said that he was faking,

1177
01:27:05,750 --> 01:27:07,800
just that his condition was mental, not physical.

1178
01:27:08,149 --> 01:27:11,138
I found out later that she went home and gave Sammy his final exam.

1179
01:27:12,720 --> 01:27:13,479
Sammy?

1180
01:27:14,389 --> 01:27:15,378
It's time for my shot.

1181
01:27:31,639 --> 01:27:33,228
She knew beyond a doubt that he loved her.

1182
01:27:34,670 --> 01:27:36,129
So she found a way to test him.

1183
01:27:49,189 --> 01:27:50,138
Sammy.

1184
01:27:51,589 --> 01:27:52,988
It's time for my shot.

1185
01:28:03,399 --> 01:28:04,799
She really thought she'd call his bluff.

1186
01:28:05,139 --> 01:28:06,038
There you go.

1187
01:28:07,139 --> 01:28:10,739
Or she just didn't wanna live with the things she put him through.

1188
01:28:21,289 --> 01:28:22,218
Sammy.

1189
01:28:24,189 --> 01:28:25,489
It's time for my shot.

1190
01:28:32,299 --> 01:28:33,419
It won't hurt.

1191
01:29:17,979 --> 01:29:19,669
She went into a coma and never recovered.

1192
01:29:20,810 --> 01:29:23,870
Sammy couldn't understand or explain what happened.

1193
01:29:26,489 --> 01:29:27,918
He's been in a home ever since.

1194
01:29:28,289 --> 01:29:29,948
He doesn't even know that his wife's dead.

1195
01:29:30,820 --> 01:29:34,059
I was wrong about Sammy, and I was wrong about his wife.

1196
01:29:34,329 --> 01:29:37,918
She wasn't interested in the money. She just needed to understand his problem.

1197
01:29:38,629 --> 01:29:40,498
His brain didn't respond to conditioning.

1198
01:29:40,800 --> 01:29:41,929
But he wasn't a con man.

1199
01:29:42,239 --> 01:29:45,329
And when she looked into his eyes, she thought he could be the same person.

1200
01:29:45,770 --> 01:29:48,069
When I looked into his eyes, I thought I saw recognition.

1201
01:29:48,509 --> 01:29:49,809
Now I know. You fake it.

1202
01:29:50,339 --> 01:29:52,938
If you're supposed to recognize somebody, you just pretend to.

1203
01:29:53,209 --> 01:29:55,239
You bluff it to get a pat on the head from the doctors.

1204
01:29:56,249 --> 01:29:58,238
You bluff it to seem less of a freak.

1205
01:30:02,389 --> 01:30:03,409
What drug dealer?

1206
01:30:08,659 --> 01:30:11,889
“事实6：车牌 SG1371U”

1207
01:30:12,299 --> 01:30:13,928
“纹身店”

1208
01:30:14,529 --> 01:30:17,368
“事实6：车牌…”

1209
01:30:29,720 --> 01:30:30,909
Hey, Lenny, how you doing?

1210
01:30:31,219 --> 01:30:32,279
It's private back here.

1211
01:30:32,619 --> 01:30:34,108
It's okay. We know each other. Right, kid?

1212
01:30:34,449 --> 01:30:35,318
How did you know I was here?

1213
01:30:35,659 --> 01:30:37,889
Oh, the Jag is out front. You should have put it around back.

1214
01:30:38,159 --> 01:30:39,279
What are you still doing here?

1215
01:30:39,629 --> 01:30:41,178
There's plenty of tattoo parlors up north.

1216
01:30:41,559 --> 01:30:42,819
I just wanted to get something down...

1217
01:30:43,129 --> 01:30:44,058
before it slipped my mind.

1218
01:30:44,329 --> 01:30:45,629
Then give me the keys. I'll move it for you.

1219
01:30:45,770 --> 01:30:47,289
-It'll be all right for a minute. -Wait out there.

1220
01:30:48,069 --> 01:30:48,859
Oh, for Christ...

1221
01:30:49,199 --> 01:30:51,028
Look, give me a minute. I gotta get something for you.

1222
01:30:55,109 --> 01:30:59,098
Fact six. Car license SG 137IU.

1223
01:31:05,589 --> 01:31:07,679
Look. Wait a minute, will ya?

1224
01:31:11,119 --> 01:31:12,519
All right, we gotta get you out of here.

1225
01:31:12,860 --> 01:31:13,849
-Why? -Aw, man.

1226
01:31:14,089 --> 01:31:16,249
Come on, Leonard. How many times I gotta tell you?

1227
01:31:16,499 --> 01:31:18,148
It's not safe for you to hang around here anymore.

1228
01:31:18,399 --> 01:31:18,958
Why not?

1229
01:31:19,029 --> 01:31:20,699
Because that cop's looking for you.

1230
01:31:20,969 --> 01:31:26,159
Now, I gotta get you a new identity, some new clothes. A different car would do for now. So put these on.

1231
01:31:26,239 --> 01:31:27,599
Whoa, whoa. What cop?

1232
01:31:28,909 --> 01:31:32,109
He's a bad cop. He's the one who checked you into the Discount Inn.

1233
01:31:32,379 --> 01:31:33,399
He's been calling you for days,

1234
01:31:33,609 --> 01:31:35,769
telling you shit, slipping envelopes under your door.

1235
01:31:35,949 --> 01:31:36,639
How do you know this?

1236
01:31:36,880 --> 01:31:39,779
He told me. He thinks it's funny. He's been laughing at you.

1237
01:31:40,149 --> 01:31:40,639
You're full of shit.

1238
01:31:40,919 --> 01:31:43,649
I'm not. He knows you're no good on the phone, so he's been calling you up.

1239
01:31:43,959 --> 01:31:45,019
Sometimes you don't answer the phone,

1240
01:31:45,359 --> 01:31:48,208
so he slips shit under your door to scare you into answering the phone again,

1241
01:31:48,479 --> 01:31:51,358
giving you a line of crap about John G. Being some local drug dealer.

1242
01:31:51,629 --> 01:31:52,598
Jimmy Grants.

1243
01:31:53,800 --> 01:31:54,629
Who's Jimmy Grants?

1244
01:31:54,899 --> 01:31:56,929
Leonard, Jimmy's the drug dealer.

1245
01:31:57,199 --> 01:31:59,299
The cop wants to know how his operation's run.

1246
01:31:59,439 --> 01:32:01,599
He's got some score in mind. Somehow you're involved.

1247
01:32:01,209 --> 01:32:02,299
How do you know him?

1248
01:32:03,009 --> 01:32:05,809
I'm a snitch. He's a cop from out of town.

1249
01:32:05,949 --> 01:32:07,309
The local boys put us together.

1250
01:32:07,750 --> 01:32:09,880
If he knew I was helping you, he'd fucking kill me.

1251
01:32:10,179 --> 01:32:12,569
So take these clothes, put them on

1252
01:32:12,750 --> 01:32:14,149
and get the fuck out of here.

1253
01:32:14,659 --> 01:32:16,178
Come on, Leonard. Just go.

1254
01:32:30,039 --> 01:32:32,429
“泰迪” “555O134”

1255
01:32:33,870 --> 01:32:36,099
“不要受他骗”

1256
01:32:37,539 --> 01:32:38,528
You are full of shit.

1257
01:32:41,249 --> 01:32:43,269
"Come by after. Natalie."

1258
01:32:43,679 --> 01:32:44,618
"Ferdy's Bar."

1259
01:33:18,589 --> 01:33:19,679
“费迪斯酒吧”

1260
01:33:27,860 --> 01:33:28,659
Hey, Jimmy.

1261
01:33:31,999 --> 01:33:35,958
I'm sorry. I, uh, thought you were somebody else. Sorry.

1262
01:33:37,740 --> 01:33:38,639
That's okay.

1263
01:33:47,750 --> 01:33:49,199
“下班后来找娜塔莉娅”

1264
01:33:53,049 --> 01:33:56,048
So this Jimmy Grants deals drugs out of the bar where his girlfriend works?

1265
01:33:57,259 --> 01:33:59,419
But he's not gonna bring her along. He'll come by himself, right?

1266
01:34:00,860 --> 01:34:03,229
I always figured the drugs angle would be the best way to get him.

1267
01:34:04,870 --> 01:34:07,890
No, officer. I'm as ready as I'll ever be.

1268
01:34:08,899 --> 01:34:09,829
You're in the lobby?

1269
01:34:10,840 --> 01:34:11,629
What do you look like?

1270
01:34:12,840 --> 01:34:13,669
I'll be right there.

1271
01:34:56,979 --> 01:34:57,849
Lenny.

1272
01:35:01,159 --> 01:35:02,179
Officer Gammell.

1273
01:35:05,029 --> 01:35:06,819
Yeah. Come on.

1274
01:35:23,639 --> 01:35:24,298
Hey, smile.

1275
01:35:24,579 --> 01:35:26,208
Oh, don't... Not here.

1276
01:35:27,509 --> 01:35:28,168
Over here.

1277
01:35:34,890 --> 01:35:37,119
Now, is it Officer or Lieutenant Gammell?

1278
01:35:37,159 --> 01:35:39,689
